msgstr "Items"

#: assets/resources/translations/handbook/keep_plants_alive.tres
msgid "KEEP_PLANTS_ALIVE"
msgstr "Keep Plants Alive"

#: assets/resources/translations/handbook/keep_plants_alive_description.tres
msgid "KEEP_PLANTS_ALIVE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Explanation how to keep your plants alive"

#: assets/resources/translations/handbook/keep_plants_alive_explain_icons.tres
msgid "BASIC_PLANT_ICON_EXPLANATION"
msgstr ""
"The water icon tells you that your plant is thirsty, go and give it some "
"water\n"
"The fertilize icon will tell you that you need to add more fertilizer to "
"your plant\n"
"The hearth icon tells you that the plant is about to die, fix the other two "
"icons to prevent this, you can also harvest the plant if it is already fully "
"grown."

#: assets/resources/translations/handbook/plants_groups.tres
msgid "PLANTS_GROUP"
msgstr "Plants"

#: assets/resources/translations/handbook/quality_entry.tres
msgid "QUALITY_ENTRY"
msgstr "Item Quality"

#: assets/resources/translations/handbook/quality_entry_description.tres
msgid "QUALITY_DESCRIPTION_ENTRY"
msgstr "What is item quality? What does it do?"

#: assets/resources/translations/handbook/quality_entry_text.tres
msgid "QUALITY_HANDBOOK_TEXT"
msgstr ""
"Most items do have a quality level, this defines if a plant has more yield "
"or requires less water. Also the chance to get higher quality drops is "
"increased. A high quality drop will give you more money as a poor one.\n"
"Also high quality fertilizer will provide more fertilizer as one with less "
"quality.\n"
"\n"
"The quality levels are Poor, Standard and Premium, check then out below"

#: assets/resources/translations/handbook/water.tres
msgid "WATER"
msgstr "Water"

#: assets/resources/translations/handbook/water_handbook_description.tres
msgid "WATER_HANDBOOK_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Plant really do need water?"

#: assets/resources/translations/handbook/water_handbook_text.tres
msgid "WATER_HANDBOOK_TEXT"
msgstr ""
"Water is needed to [url={\"entry\":\"KeepPlantAlive\"}]keep your plants "
"alive[/url]. Plants will user water all the time and die if not enough is "
"available.\n"
"To water your plants you will need a water can, the [url={\"entry\":"
"\"OLD_WATER_CAN_NAME_POOR\"}]old water can[/url] is the first one you get. "
"You should fill them up at the well.\n"
"Keep your plant pots always filled with water."

#: assets/resources/translations/items/fertilizer_description.tres
msgid "FERTILIZER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Use this to fertilize the ground, allowing you to continue growing plants"

#: assets/resources/translations/items/fertilizer_name.tres
msgid "FERTILIZER_NAME"
msgstr "Fertilizer"

#: assets/resources/translations/items/old_water_can_description.tres
msgid "OLD_WATER_CAN_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "That's my old rusty water can, should be fine to start with"

#: assets/resources/translations/items/old_water_can_long_description.tres
msgid "OLD_WATER_CAN_LONG_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"I got this water can gifted as a child, I kept it for years now. It's in a "
"really bad shape, but still holds water without leaking.\vI can use this to "
"[url={\"entry\":\"Water\"}]water[/url] my plants."

#: assets/resources/translations/items/old_water_can_name.tres
msgid "OLD_WATER_CAN_NAME"
msgstr "Old Water Can"

#: assets/resources/translations/plants/corn_description.tres
msgid "CORN_PLANT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This is a corn plant, put it into one of the pots to grow it, this plant "
"does drop some corn if fully grown\n"
"Do not forget to water the plant and keep it fertilized"

#: assets/resources/translations/plants/corn_name.tres
msgid "CORN_PLANT_NAME"
msgstr "Corn plant"

#: assets/resources/translations/plants/dead_plant_description.tres
msgid "DEAD_PLANT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This plant is dead, either there wasn't enough nutrition or water available "
"to keep it alive"

#: assets/resources/translations/plants/dead_plant_name.tres
msgid "DEAD_PLANT_NAME"
msgstr "Dead Plant"

#: assets/resources/translations/plants/rose_plant_description.tres
msgid "ROSE_PLANT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A rose plant, it does take a while to grow that plant, but the yield is "
"worth the trouble. At least that's what I heared"

#: assets/resources/translations/plants/rose_plant_name.tres
msgid "ROSE_PLANT_NAME"
msgstr "Rose flower"

#: assets/resources/translations/settings/vsync/vsync_adaptive.tres
